---
status: 'published';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Planning - Think through your website before building"
  description="A concise planning guide to clarify what your website should do, who it serves, what belongs in the first version, and how it may evolve."
>
  <!-- Intro -->
  <section class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-950">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-20 md:py-28">
      <p
        class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300 mb-2"
      >
        Guides
      </p>
      <h1
        class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-serif font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4"
      >
        Planning
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 max-w-3xl">
        You know you need a website. Now the question is what it should do.
        Planning does not mean having every answer in advance. It means getting
        clear enough to choose the right first version.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How to use this + Figure -->
  <section
    class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-950 border-t border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800"
  >
    <div
      class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 md:py-16 grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 md:gap-12 items-start"
    >
      <div>
        <h2
          class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4"
        >
          Use this to prepare for the conversation.
        </h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 mb-4">
          This page is not meant to become homework. It is a way to notice the
          decisions that matter most before a website takes shape.
        </p>
        <div
          class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
        >
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            <li>Answer briefly. A sentence or two is enough.</li>
            <li>Focus on what the site needs to accomplish first.</li>
            <li>Bring rough notes, examples, links, or questions.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <figure
        class="relative rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800"
      >
        <img
          src="/images/guides/circle-pattern-black-white.webp"
          alt="Abstract circle pattern suggesting structure and relationships"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
          class="w-full h-full object-cover"
        />
        <figcaption class="sr-only">Visual: abstract structure map</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What should the site do? -->
  <section class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-950">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 md:py-16">
      <h2
        class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4"
      >
        What should the site do?
      </h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 mb-6 max-w-3xl">
        Every website exists to help someone take a step. The step might be
        booking a call, understanding your work, visiting a location, reading
        more, making a purchase, or deciding you are credible.
      </p>

      <div class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6">
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
          <li>
            What should a first-time visitor understand within thirty seconds?
          </li>
          <li>What action should they take next?</li>
          <li>What would make the site successful in the next 90 days?</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Who is it for? -->
  <section
    class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-950 border-t border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800"
  >
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 md:py-16">
      <h2
        class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4"
      >
        Who is it for?
      </h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 mb-6 max-w-3xl">
        A website works better when it speaks clearly to the people it is meant
        to serve. You do not need to define everyone. You need a useful sense of
        who matters most.
      </p>

      <div class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6">
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
          <li>Who is the site primarily for?</li>
          <li>What are they trying to understand, solve, or decide?</li>
          <li>What would help them trust you enough to take the next step?</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What belongs in the first version? -->
  <section class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-950">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 md:py-16">
      <h2
        class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4"
      >
        What belongs in the first version?
      </h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 mb-6 max-w-3xl">
        Many website projects become harder than they need to be because
        everything is treated as equally important. A strong first version gives
        the site a clear job and leaves room to grow.
      </p>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <article
          class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
            Needs to launch
          </h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            The pages, sections, or details the site needs in order to be useful
            immediately.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article
          class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
            Can wait
          </h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            Good ideas that may matter later, but do not need to slow down the
            first version.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article
          class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
            Might not belong
          </h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            Features, pages, or flourishes that add complexity without helping
            the visitor.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Decorative band -->
  <div class="relative">
    <img
      src="/images/guides/dots-blue-yellow-tws-thin.webp"
      alt=""
      loading="lazy"
      decoding="async"
      class="w-full h-24 object-cover opacity-80 dark:opacity-70"
    />
    <div
      class="absolute inset-0 ring-1 ring-stone-200/70 dark:ring-stone-800/70 pointer-events-none"
    >
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- What proof already exists? -->
  <section class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-950">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 md:py-16">
      <h2
        class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4"
      >
        What proof already exists?
      </h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 mb-6 max-w-3xl">
        You may already have more useful material than you think. A first
        version of a website is often shaped from existing examples, messages,
        images, notes, and conversations.
      </p>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <article
          class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
            Useful material
          </h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            <li>Client messages and common questions.</li>
            <li>Testimonials, reviews, or informal praise.</li>
            <li>
              Project examples, photos, outcomes, or before-and-after notes.
            </li>
            <li>
              Presentations, proposals, posts, talks, articles, or drafts.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article
          class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
            Questions to ask
          </h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            <li>What examples best show the quality of the work?</li>
            <li>What do people usually ask before they are ready?</li>
            <li>What existing material could be reused or reshaped?</li>
            <li>What is missing, but important enough to create?</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How will the site evolve? -->
  <section
    class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-950 border-t border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800"
  >
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 md:py-16">
      <h2
        class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4"
      >
        How will the site evolve?
      </h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 mb-6 max-w-3xl">
        Some sites stay mostly stable for years. Others grow through articles,
        events, resources, new projects, or changing offers. The expected rhythm
        affects the structure and the tools.
      </p>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <article
          class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
            Mostly stable
          </h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            Best when the site mainly needs to explain who you are, what you do,
            and how to begin.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article
          class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
            Occasionally updated
          </h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            Good for adding new proof, changing offers, updating photos, or
            improving copy over time.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article
          class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
            Actively maintained
          </h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            Useful when publishing, events, resources, memberships, or ongoing
            communication are central to the site.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Before we talk -->
  <section class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-950">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 md:py-16">
      <h2
        class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4"
      >
        Before we talk
      </h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 mb-6 max-w-3xl">
        You do not need a complete plan. A few rough answers are enough to begin
        a useful conversation.
      </p>

      <div
        class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6 md:p-8"
      >
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
          <li>What should the site help people understand or do?</li>
          <li>Who matters most as the audience?</li>
          <li>What examples, links, images, or materials already exist?</li>
          <li>What feels confusing, missing, or unresolved?</li>
          <li>What would make this project worthwhile in the next 90 days?</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 mt-6 max-w-3xl">
        Bring your ideas, questions, examples, rough notes, or half-formed
        thoughts. We can shape the rest together.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Next steps -->
  <section
    class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-950 border-t border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800"
  >
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 md:py-20">
      <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-4">
        <a
          href="/guides"
          class="inline-block bg-blue-700 text-white px-6 py-3 rounded-lg font-semibold hover:bg-blue-800 transition dark:bg-blue-500 dark:hover:bg-blue-400"
        >
          Back to Guides
        </a>
        <a
          href="/guides/web-builders"
          class="inline-block border border-blue-700 text-blue-700 px-6 py-3 rounded-lg font-semibold hover:bg-blue-50 transition dark:border-blue-300 dark:text-blue-300 dark:hover:bg-blue-900/30"
        >
          Read Platform Overview
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="text-center text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mt-3">
        The plan does not need to be perfect. It just needs to be clear enough
        to start.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
